    "narrative": "Today\u2019s offensive engine is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29), who stands as our premier play against Scherzer. The matchup is favorable given the SP\u2019s xERA of 5.10, but the efficiency boost is driven by the specific synergy between **Gunnar Henderson**'s elite sprint speed and a pitcher known for a slower delivery, creating a high-upside environment for stolen bases. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (75.93) and **Kyle Tucker** (68.82) also anchor the heart of the order; while they face respectable arms, their high base projections combined with advantageous order spots in the 3 and 4 holes guarantee stable production. **Jackson Merrill** (60.45) warrants attention as well\u2014despite a marginal park factor, the wind blowing out at the stadium serves as a catalyst to elevate him into \"Strong\" start territory.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Tommy White**, who produced a solid 49.41 score. He benefited significantly from a 10% park factor bump against Kirby, but ultimately lacked the efficiency floor provided by the middle-of-the-order anchors. We are also monitoring **Wade Meckler** (42.38) closely; while he earns the start due to a platoon advantage, his score remains dangerously close to the 40-point \"Below Floor\" threshold due to the high-skill profile of the opposing pitcher. We continue to manage our bench depth with **Liam Hicks** (38.30) remaining on the pine, as his performance metrics against a tough SP matchup failed to clear our 40-point minimum threshold. Investors should note that while **Drake Baldwin** (57.21) provides solid production from the leadoff spot, we are operating with limited roster flexibility while **Jordan Westburg** and **Andy Pages** remain sidelined on the IL, placing additional pressure on our secondary options like **Miguel Vargas** to maximize their plate appearances.",
